{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:0.3"], "en": "Chapter on the Bīraṇa Thicket (Bīraṇathambhavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:0.4"], "en": "5. The Kacchapajātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:1.1", "PA_ja_215:1.2"], "en": "“Alas, the tortoise has brought destruction upon himself by uttering a voice!”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:1.3"], "en": "When the wood was firmly grasped,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:1.4"], "en": "it was severed by a single word.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:2.1"], "en": "Having seen this too, O best among men in valor, [you should exert yourself].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:2.2"], "en": "Let forth speech that is wholesome, but not excessively;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:2.3"], "en": "do you not see how the tortoise,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:2.4"], "en": "through much talking, has come to ruin?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_215:3.1"], "en": "The Kacchapajātaka, the fifth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
]
